<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<tbx type="TBX-Basic" style="dca" xml:lang="en" xmlns="urn:iso:std:iso:30042:ed-2">
<tbxHeader><fileDesc><sourceDesc><p>Diffusion Works — Lithium-ion Battery Manufacturing Termbase — evaluation sample (50 terms). Non-commercial evaluation use only.</p></sourceDesc></fileDesc></tbxHeader>
<text><body>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-00006"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / active-materials</descrip><descrip type="definition">Electrode of a cell that is at the higher potential; in a lithium-ion cell it holds the lithium metal oxide or phosphate active material on aluminum foil.</descrip><admin type="source">IEC 60050-482 (International Electrotechnical Vocabulary - Part 482: Primary and secondary cells and batteries); M. Yoshio, R. J. Brodd, A. Kozawa (eds.), Lithium-Ion Batteries: Science and Technologies (Springer, 2009)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>positive electrode</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>cathode</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>正極</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>陰極</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「陰極」(JA) は cathode の辞書訳で、日本語の電池分野では負側の電極と受け取られ、リチウムイオン電池の正極と極性が逆に読まれる。韓国語の「음극」は電池業界では負極（anode）を指すため、cathode の訳に使うと正負が逆になる。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>正极</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>양극</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>음극</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「陰極」(JA) は cathode の辞書訳で、日本語の電池分野では負側の電極と受け取られ、リチウムイオン電池の正極と極性が逆に読まれる。韓国語の「음극」は電池業界では負極（anode）を指すため、cathode の訳に使うと正負が逆になる。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>positive Elektrode</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Kathode</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>electrodo positivo</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>cátodo</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-00040"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / active-materials</descrip><descrip type="definition">Cathode material designed to operate at potentials above about 4.3 V vs Li/Li+, such as LNMO or high-voltage LCO, to raise cell energy.</descrip><admin type="source">A. Manthiram, A reflection on lithium-ion battery cathode chemistry, Nat. Commun. 11 (2020) 1550</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>high-voltage cathode</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>high-voltage cathode material</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>高電位正極材</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>高電圧正極材</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>高电压正极材料</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>고전압 양극재</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>고전압 음극</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>韓国語の「고전압 음극」は cathode を辞書訳の「음극」としたもので、電池業界では負極と読まれ、正極材とは正負が逆になる。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Hochvolt-Kathodenmaterial</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Hochvoltkathode</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>cátodo de alto voltaje</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-00043"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / recycling-regulation</descrip><descrip type="definition">Cathode layer of an all-solid-state cell in which cathode active material is mixed with solid electrolyte and conductive additive so that ions and electrons can reach every particle.</descrip><admin type="source">Schnell et al., All-solid-state lithium-ion and lithium metal batteries — paving the way to large-scale production, J. Power Sources 382, 160–175 (2018)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>composite cathode</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>複合正極</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>正極複合体</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>复合正极</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>복합 양극</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>복합 음극</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>韓国語の「복합 음극」は cathode を辞書訳の「음극」としたもので、電池業界では複合負極と読まれ、正負が逆になる。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Kompositkathode</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>cátodo compuesto</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>cátodo compósito</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-00229"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / testing-characterization</descrip><descrip type="definition">Test cell with a reference electrode in addition to the positive and negative electrodes, so that the potential of each electrode can be measured separately during cycling or impedance tests.</descrip><admin type="source">Korthauer (ed.), Lithium-Ion Batteries: Basics and Applications, Springer (2018)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>three-electrode cell</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>three-electrode setup</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>三極セル</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>三電極セル</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>三电极电池</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>三电极体系</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>3전극 셀</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>삼전극 셀</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Dreielektrodenzelle</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Drei-Elektroden-Zelle</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>celda de tres electrodos</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-00290"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / recycling-regulation</descrip><descrip type="definition">Raw material designated by the EU as economically important and at high supply risk, a list that includes lithium, cobalt, natural graphite and battery-grade nickel, triggering sourcing, stockpiling and recycling measures.</descrip><admin type="source">Regulation (EU) 2024/1252 (Critical Raw Materials Act)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>critical raw material</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>CRM</term><termNote type="termType">abbreviation</termNote><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>重要原材料</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>关键原材料</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>핵심원자재</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>핵심 원자재</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>kritischer Rohstoff</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>materia prima crítica</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-00306"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / active-materials</descrip><descrip type="definition">Method that forces mercury into a porous sample at increasing pressure and converts the intruded volume into a pore size distribution and porosity, applied to electrodes, separators and powders.</descrip><admin type="source">ISO 15901-1 (Pore size distribution and porosity of solid materials by mercury porosimetry and gas adsorption - Part 1: Mercury porosimetry); ISO 15901-1 Pore size distribution and porosity of solid materials by mercury porosimetry and gas adsorption - Part 1: Mercury porosimetry</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>mercury porosimetry</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>mercury intrusion porosimetry</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>MIP</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>水銀圧入法</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>水銀ポロシメトリー</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>压汞法</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>수은 압입법</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Quecksilberporosimetrie</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Quecksilberintrusion</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>porosimetría de mercurio</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>porosimetría por intrusión de mercurio</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>porosimetría de intrusión de mercurio</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-00367"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / inactive-materials</descrip><descrip type="definition">Cyclic ester (lactone) solvent with high permittivity, a high boiling point and a low melting point, used in some lithium-ion and lithium primary electrolytes.</descrip><admin type="source">K. Xu, Nonaqueous liquid electrolytes for lithium-based rechargeable batteries, Chem. Rev. 104 (2004) 4303</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>gamma-butyrolactone</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>GBL</term><termNote type="termType">abbreviation</termNote><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>γ-butyrolactone</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>γ-ブチロラクトン</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>ガンマブチロラクトン</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>γ-丁内酯</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>감마-부티로락톤</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>γ-부티로락톤</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>γ-Butyrolacton</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>gamma-Butyrolacton</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>γ-butirolactona</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>gamma-butirolactona</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-00448"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / inactive-materials</descrip><descrip type="definition">Polymer in the electrode coating that binds active and conductive particles to each other and to the current collector foil, such as PVDF for cathodes or SBR/CMC for anodes.</descrip><admin type="source">H. Chen et al., Exploring chemical, mechanical, and electrical functionalities of binders for advanced energy-storage devices, Chem. Rev. 118 (2018) 8936</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>binder</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>バインダー</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>バインダ</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>結着剤</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>結着材</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>粘结剂</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>黏结剂</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>活页夹</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>中国語「活页夹」、ドイツ語「Ordner」、スペイン語「carpeta」は書類を綴じるバインダー（ファイル）の意味で、電極の結着剤には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>바인더</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>결합제</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Binder</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Bindemittel</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Ordner</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>中国語「活页夹」、ドイツ語「Ordner」、スペイン語「carpeta」は書類を綴じるバインダー（ファイル）の意味で、電極の結着剤には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>aglutinante</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>ligante</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>carpeta</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>中国語「活页夹」、ドイツ語「Ordner」、スペイン語「carpeta」は書類を綴じるバインダー（ファイル）の意味で、電極の結着剤には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-00482"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / inactive-materials</descrip><descrip type="definition">Metal foil, normally copper, that carries the negative active material layer and conducts current to the negative tab.</descrip><admin type="source">Furukawa Electric: electrodeposited copper foil for lithium-ion batteries public page</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>anode current collector</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>negative current collector</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>負極集電体</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>陽極集電体</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>日本語の「陽極集電体」は anode を電気分解の陽極（プラス側）と字面訳したもので、電池では anode は負極と訳す。韓国語「양극」は電池では正極を意味するため、「양극 집전체」は正極集電体になる。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>负极集流体</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>음극 집전체</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>양극 집전체</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>日本語の「陽極集電体」は anode を電気分解の陽極（プラス側）と字面訳したもので、電池では anode は負極と訳す。韓国語「양극」は電池では正極を意味するため、「양극 집전체」は正極集電体になる。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Anodenstromableiter</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>colector de corriente del ánodo</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>colector de corriente negativo</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-00548"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / mixing-slurry</descrip><descrip type="definition">Electrode slurry for the negative electrode, typically graphite, sometimes blended with silicon, with conductive additive and CMC/SBR binders dispersed in water.</descrip><admin type="source">PEM RWTH Aachen &amp; VDMA Battery Production, Production of Lithium-Ion Battery Cell Components (brochure)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>anode slurry</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>negative electrode slurry</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>負極スラリー</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>負極合材スラリー</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>陽極スラリー</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>日本語「陽極スラリー」は anode を電気分解などの陽極と字面どおりに訳したもので、日本語の電池分野では正極側と読まれる。韓国語「양극 슬러리」は電池では正極スラリーを意味し、負極とは正負が逆になる。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>负极浆料</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>음극 슬러리</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>양극 슬러리</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>日本語「陽極スラリー」は anode を電気分解などの陽極と字面どおりに訳したもので、日本語の電池分野では正極側と読まれる。韓国語「양극 슬러리」は電池では正極スラリーを意味し、負極とは正負が逆になる。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Anodenslurry</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Anodenpaste</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>suspensión anódica</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>slurry anódico</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-00646"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / mixing-slurry</descrip><descrip type="definition">Loading of the raw materials for a slurry batch, powders and liquids, into the mixer in the specified amounts and order.</descrip><admin type="source">PEM RWTH Aachen &amp; VDMA Battery Production, Production of Lithium-Ion Battery Cell Components (brochure)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>material charging</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>raw material charging</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>material feeding</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>原料投入</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>材料投入</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>充電</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「充電」（中国語「充电」）は電池に電気を充電する意味で、ミキサーへ原料を入れる操作には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>投料</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>加料</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>充电</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「充電」（中国語「充电」）は電池に電気を充電する意味で、ミキサーへ原料を入れる操作には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>원료 투입</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>재료 투입</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Materialzugabe</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Beschickung</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>carga de material</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>alimentación de material</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-00723"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / mixing-slurry</descrip><descrip type="definition">Gradual change in the pH of an aqueous electrode slurry during storage, for example a rise caused by lithium leaching from nickel-rich cathode particles.</descrip><admin type="source">Hawley &amp; Li, Electrode manufacturing for lithium-ion batteries, J. Energy Storage 25 (2019)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>pH drift</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>pH経時変化</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>pHドリフト</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>pH值漂移</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>pH漂移</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>pH 드리프트</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>pH-Drift</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>pH-Wert-Drift</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>deriva del pH</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-00805"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / coating-drying</descrip><descrip type="definition">Technique used to apply the electrode slurry or another liquid layer onto the substrate, such as slot-die, comma, gravure or roll coating.</descrip><admin type="source">Cohen &amp; Gutoff, Modern Coating and Drying Technology, Wiley-VCH (1992)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>coating method</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>coating technique</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>塗工方式</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>涂布方式</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>코팅 방식</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Beschichtungsverfahren</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>método de recubrimiento</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-00910"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / coating-drying</descrip><descrip type="definition">Enclosed, usually multi-zone section of an electrode coating line in which heated air removes the solvent from the wet coating as the web passes through.</descrip><admin type="source">Duerr, battery electrode coating and drying systems (public product page); Cohen &amp; Gutoff, Modern Coating and Drying Technology, Wiley-VCH (1992)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>drying oven</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>dryer</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>乾燥炉</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>乾燥機</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>ドライヤー</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>ドライルーム</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「ドライルーム」（日本語）・「干燥房」（中国語）・「드라이룸」（韓国語）・「Trockenraum」（ドイツ語）・「sala seca」（スペイン語）は低露点に保つ作業室（dry room）で、塗工機の乾燥炉とは別の設備。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>烘箱</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>干燥机</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>干燥房</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「ドライルーム」（日本語）・「干燥房」（中国語）・「드라이룸」（韓国語）・「Trockenraum」（ドイツ語）・「sala seca」（スペイン語）は低露点に保つ作業室（dry room）で、塗工機の乾燥炉とは別の設備。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>건조로</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>건조 오븐</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>건조기</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>드라이룸</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「ドライルーム」（日本語）・「干燥房」（中国語）・「드라이룸」（韓国語）・「Trockenraum」（ドイツ語）・「sala seca」（スペイン語）は低露点に保つ作業室（dry room）で、塗工機の乾燥炉とは別の設備。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Trockenofen</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Trockner</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Trockenraum</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「ドライルーム」（日本語）・「干燥房」（中国語）・「드라이룸」（韓国語）・「Trockenraum」（ドイツ語）・「sala seca」（スペイン語）は低露点に保つ作業室（dry room）で、塗工機の乾燥炉とは別の設備。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>horno de secado</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>secador</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>secadero</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>sala seca</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「ドライルーム」（日本語）・「干燥房」（中国語）・「드라이룸」（韓国語）・「Trockenraum」（ドイツ語）・「sala seca」（スペイン語）は低露点に保つ作業室（dry room）で、塗工機の乾燥炉とは別の設備。</note></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01063"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / coating-drying</descrip><descrip type="definition">Electrode coating layer left on the foil after the solvent has been removed in the dryer, before calendering.</descrip><admin type="source">ISO 2808 Paints and varnishes - Determination of film thickness</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>dry film</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>乾燥塗膜</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>乾燥膜</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>ドライフィルム</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>日本語の「ドライフィルム」はプリント基板製造に使う感光性のドライフィルムレジストを指す語で、乾燥後の電極塗膜には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>干膜</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>干涂层</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>건조 도막</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Trockenschicht</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Trockenfilm</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>película seca</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01066"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / calendering-slitting</descrip><descrip type="definition">Machine with two or more heated, precision-ground rolls that compacts the dried electrode coating to the target thickness and density as the web runs through the nip.</descrip><admin type="source">PEM RWTH Aachen / VDMA: Production process of a lithium-ion battery cell (public process guide); Matthews International (Saueressig): battery electrode calender (public product page)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>calender</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>roll press</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>calender press</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>ロールプレス機</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>ロールプレス装置</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>辊压机</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>롤 프레스</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Kalander</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>calandra</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>satinadora</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>スペイン語の「satinadora」は紙・布の表面につやを出す仕上げ用カレンダーを指し、電極を圧密するロールプレス機には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01129"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / safety-abuse</descrip><descrip type="definition">Manually initiated function that brings a production machine, such as a winder, stacker or formation line, to a stop as quickly as is safe in order to avert or limit danger.</descrip><admin type="source">IEC 60204-1 Safety of machinery - Electrical equipment of machines - Part 1: General requirements; ISO 13850 Safety of machinery - Emergency stop function - Principles for design</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>emergency stop</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>E-stop</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>emergency stop function</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>非常停止</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>緊急停止</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>紧急停止</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>急停</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>비상 정지</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>비상정지</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Not-Halt</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Nothalt</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>parada de emergencia</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>desconexión de emergencia</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「desconexión de emergencia」（スペイン語）は電源を断つ非常遮断（emergency switching off）の語で、機械の動きを止める非常停止とは別概念。</note></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01132"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / calendering-slitting</descrip><descrip type="definition">Machine that unwinds the electrode parent roll, slits it lengthwise with knives or laser and rewinds the strips onto separate cores.</descrip><admin type="source">PEM RWTH Aachen / VDMA: Production process of a lithium-ion battery cell (public process guide); Kampf Schneid- und Wickeltechnik: slitter rewinders for battery electrodes (public product pages)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>slitter</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>slitting machine</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>slitter rewinder</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>スリッター</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>スリッタ</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>分切机</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>分条机</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>슬리터</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Längsschneidmaschine</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Rollenschneidmaschine</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>cortadora-rebobinadora</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>máquina de corte longitudinal</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01151"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / calendering-slitting</descrip><descrip type="definition">Lower, female cutting tool of a punching or notching die whose opening, together with the punch, shears the electrode.</descrip><admin type="source">Schuler GmbH, Metal Forming Handbook, Springer (1998)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>die</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>cutting die</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>ダイ</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>凹模</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>芯片</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「芯片」（中国語）は半導体のダイ（チップ）で、プレス金型のダイではない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>다이</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Matrize</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Schneidplatte</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>matriz</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01269"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / winding-stacking</descrip><descrip type="definition">Machine that stacks cut cathode and anode sheets with separator into an electrode stack, by single-sheet, Z-folding or lamination methods.</descrip><admin type="source">PEM RWTH Aachen / VDMA: Production process of a lithium-ion battery cell (public process guide); Manz AG: battery cell assembly - notching, cutting, stacking, lamination (public product pages)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>stacking machine</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>electrode stacking machine</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>積層機</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>積層装置</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>電極積層機</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>叠片机</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>堆垛机</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>中国語の「堆垛机」は倉庫でパレットや荷を積み上げる搬送設備（スタッカークレーン）を指し、電極シートを積層する積層機ではない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>스태킹 장비</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>적층기</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>적층 장비</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Stapelmaschine</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Stapelanlage</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>apiladora</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>máquina de apilado</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01336"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / quality-inspection</descrip><descrip type="definition">Groove melted into the base metal along the toe of a weld and left unfilled, which reduces the cross-section and acts as a notch, for example in laser welds of busbars or can lids.</descrip><admin type="source">ISO 6520-1 Welding and allied processes - Classification of geometric imperfections in metallic materials - Part 1: Fusion welding</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>undercut</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>アンダーカット</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>咬边</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>언더컷</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Einbrandkerbe</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Hinterschneidung</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>ドイツ語の「Hinterschneidung」は機械加工品や成形品のアンダーカット（えぐれ形状）を指し、溶接止端に残る溶接欠陥のアンダーカットは「Einbrandkerbe」。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>mordedura</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01340"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / winding-stacking</descrip><descrip type="definition">Droplets of molten metal thrown out of the weld pool during laser or resistance welding; in cell assembly they are conductive particles that can cause internal short circuits.</descrip><admin type="source">ISO 6520-1 Classification of geometric imperfections in metallic materials - Part 1: Fusion welding; ISO 6520-1 Welding and allied processes - Classification of geometric imperfections in metallic materials - Part 1: Fusion welding</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>spatter</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>weld spatter</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>スパッタ</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>溶接スパッタ</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>スパッタリング</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「スパッタリング」（日本語）・「溅射」（中国語）・「스퍼터링」（韓国語）は薄膜を成膜するスパッタリング（sputtering）を指す別概念で、溶接時に飛散する溶融金属の粒には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>飞溅</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>焊接飞溅</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>溅射</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「スパッタリング」（日本語）・「溅射」（中国語）・「스퍼터링」（韓国語）は薄膜を成膜するスパッタリング（sputtering）を指す別概念で、溶接時に飛散する溶融金属の粒には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>스패터</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>용접 스패터</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>스퍼터링</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「スパッタリング」（日本語）・「溅射」（中国語）・「스퍼터링」（韓国語）は薄膜を成膜するスパッタリング（sputtering）を指す別概念で、溶接時に飛散する溶融金属の粒には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Spritzer</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Schweißspritzer</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>salpicadura</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>salpicaduras</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>salpicaduras de soldadura</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>proyecciones de soldadura</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01348"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / winding-stacking</descrip><descrip type="definition">Lens-shaped zone of metal that melted and solidified at the interface between the parts in a resistance spot weld; its diameter is the main measure of joint strength.</descrip><admin type="source">AWS A3.0M/A3.0 Standard Welding Terms and Definitions</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>weld nugget</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>nugget</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>ナゲット</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>溶接ナゲット</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>熔核</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>너깃</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>용접 너깃</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Schweißlinse</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Schweißpunktlinse</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>núcleo de soldadura</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>pepita de soldadura</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01393"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / cell-packaging</descrip><descrip type="definition">Geometric type of a cell defined by its housing and electrode arrangement, mainly cylindrical, prismatic or pouch, which determines assembly processes and pack design.</descrip><admin type="source">PEM RWTH Aachen &amp; VDMA Battery Production, Production Process of a Lithium-Ion Battery Cell (brochure)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>cell format</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>form factor</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>セル形状</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>セルの書式</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>日本語の「セルの書式」、中国語の「单元格格式」、韓国語の「셀 서식」は表計算ソフトのセルの書式を指す語で、電池セルの形状の区分には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>电池封装形式</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>电芯形态</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>单元格格式</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>日本語の「セルの書式」、中国語の「单元格格式」、韓国語の「셀 서식」は表計算ソフトのセルの書式を指す語で、電池セルの形状の区分には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>셀 폼팩터</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>셀 형태</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>셀 서식</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>日本語の「セルの書式」、中国語の「单元格格式」、韓国語の「셀 서식」は表計算ソフトのセルの書式を指す語で、電池セルの形状の区分には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Zellformat</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>formato de celda</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01395"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / cell-packaging</descrip><descrip type="definition">Cell housed in a rigid rectangular metal or plastic case, usually containing a flat-wound or stacked electrode assembly.</descrip><admin type="source">IEC 61960-3 Secondary lithium cells and batteries for portable applications - Part 3: Prismatic and cylindrical lithium secondary cells and batteries made from them</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>prismatic cell</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>prismatic hard-case cell</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>角形セル</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>角形電池</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>角型セル</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>角型電池</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>方形电池</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>方形电芯</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>方形单体电池</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>각형 셀</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>각형 전지</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>prismatische Zelle</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>celda prismática</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>elemento prismático</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01474"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / cell-packaging</descrip><descrip type="definition">Electrically conductive part of a cell or battery to which external conductors are connected for charging and discharging.</descrip><admin type="source">IEC 60050-482 International Electrotechnical Vocabulary - Part 482: Primary and secondary cells and batteries</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>terminal</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>端子</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>端末</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「端末」（日本語）・「终端」（中国語）・「단말기」（韓国語）は情報機器の端末（computer terminal）の語で、電池の端子には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>端子</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>终端</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「端末」（日本語）・「终端」（中国語）・「단말기」（韓国語）は情報機器の端末（computer terminal）の語で、電池の端子には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>단자</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>단말기</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「端末」（日本語）・「终端」（中国語）・「단말기」（韓国語）は情報機器の端末（computer terminal）の語で、電池の端子には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Pol</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Anschluss</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Polanschluss</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>borne</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>terminal</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01633"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / filling-sealing</descrip><descrip type="definition">Letting gas into an evacuated chamber to bring it back to atmospheric pressure at the end of a filling or drying cycle.</descrip><admin type="source">Pfeiffer Vacuum, The Vacuum Technology Book</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>chamber venting</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>大気開放</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>チャンバーベント</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>換気</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「換気」（日本語）・「通风」（中国語）・「환기」（韓国語）は室内などの空気の入れ換えを指し、真空チャンバーにガスを入れて大気圧に戻す操作には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>破真空</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>通风</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「換気」（日本語）・「通风」（中国語）・「환기」（韓国語）は室内などの空気の入れ換えを指し、真空チャンバーにガスを入れて大気圧に戻す操作には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>대기 개방</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>진공 파기</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>환기</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「換気」（日本語）・「通风」（中国語）・「환기」（韓国語）は室内などの空気の入れ換えを指し、真空チャンバーにガスを入れて大気圧に戻す操作には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Belüften</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Kammerbelüftung</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>ventilación de la cámara</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01670"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / filling-sealing</descrip><descrip type="definition">Hole, crack, porous path or seal defect through which gas or liquid can pass from one side of a cell or housing wall to the other.</descrip><admin type="source">ISO 20484 Non-destructive testing - Leak testing - Vocabulary</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>leak</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>リーク</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>漏れ孔</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>漏液</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「漏液」（中国語「漏液」、韓国語「누액」）は電解液が外へ漏れ出す現象で、気体も通る穴・経路としてのリーク（漏孔）とは別概念。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>漏孔</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>漏液</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「漏液」（中国語「漏液」、韓国語「누액」）は電解液が外へ漏れ出す現象で、気体も通る穴・経路としてのリーク（漏孔）とは別概念。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>누설구</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>리크</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>누액</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「漏液」（中国語「漏液」、韓国語「누액」）は電解液が外へ漏れ出す現象で、気体も通る穴・経路としてのリーク（漏孔）とは別概念。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Leck</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>fuga</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01712"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / filling-sealing</descrip><descrip type="definition">Closed, usually stainless-steel tank kept under a dry nitrogen or argon blanket that holds electrolyte at the filling line and feeds the dosing pumps.</descrip><admin type="source">Wuxi Lead Intelligent Equipment, cell assembly and electrolyte filling equipment, public product pages</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>electrolyte storage tank</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>電解液タンク</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>電解液貯槽</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>电解液储罐</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>电解液罐</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>전해액 저장 탱크</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>전해액 탱크</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Elektrolyttank</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Elektrolytvorratstank</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>tanque de almacenamiento de electrolito</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>depósito de electrolito</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01795"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / formation-aging</descrip><descrip type="definition">Breakdown of electrolyte solvents and salt by reduction at the negative electrode surface at low potential, the reaction that builds the SEI.</descrip><admin type="source">Xu, Nonaqueous liquid electrolytes for lithium-based rechargeable batteries, Chem. Rev. 104 (2004)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>reductive decomposition</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>reductive electrolyte decomposition</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>還元分解</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>还原分解</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>환원 분해</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>reduktive Zersetzung</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>descomposición reductiva</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01827"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / formation-aging</descrip><descrip type="definition">Duration for which filled or formed cells are stored at a set temperature in the aging step, typically days to weeks, before OCV is measured again.</descrip><admin type="source">Wood, Li &amp; Daniel, Formation Challenges of Lithium-Ion Battery Manufacturing, Joule 3 (2019)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>aging time</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>エージング時間</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>劣化時間</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>日本語「劣化時間」・韓国語「노화 시간」は劣化が進む時間の意味になり、化成後のセルを所定温度で静置するエージング工程の時間を表さない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>老化时间</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>에이징 시간</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>노화 시간</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>日本語「劣化時間」・韓国語「노화 시간」は劣化が進む時間の意味になり、化成後のセルを所定温度で静置するエージング工程の時間を表さない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Reifelagerungsdauer</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>tiempo de envejecimiento</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01852"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / formation-aging</descrip><descrip type="definition">Physical separation of finished cells into bins or trays by grade, based on measured capacity, OCV, internal resistance and self-discharge.</descrip><admin type="source">Wood, Li &amp; Daniel, Formation Challenges of Lithium-Ion Battery Manufacturing, Joule 3 (2019); Wuxi Lead Intelligent Equipment, public formation &amp; grading / logistics equipment pages</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>sorting</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>選別</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>分选</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>排序</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>中国語「排序」・韓国語「정렬」はデータを順に並べ替える意味の sorting の訳で、セルを等級ごとに物理的に仕分ける選別には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>선별</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>정렬</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>中国語「排序」・韓国語「정렬」はデータを順に並べ替える意味の sorting の訳で、セルを等級ごとに物理的に仕分ける選別には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Zellsortierung</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>clasificación de celdas</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01895"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / testing-characterization</descrip><descrip type="definition">Capacity of a cell or battery declared by the manufacturer for a specified discharge rate, temperature and end-of-discharge voltage.</descrip><admin type="source">IEC 60050-482 International Electrotechnical Vocabulary — Part 482: Primary and secondary cells and batteries</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>rated capacity</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>定格容量</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>公称容量</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>日本語「公称容量」は電池を識別するための概略の容量値（nominal capacity）で、メーカーが規定条件で宣言する定格容量とは別概念。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>额定容量</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>정격 용량</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Bemessungskapazität</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>capacidad asignada</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-01927"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / testing-characterization</descrip><descrip type="definition">Operation in which a cell or battery delivers electric current to an external circuit, converting stored chemical energy into electrical energy.</descrip><admin type="source">IEC 60050-482 International Electrotechnical Vocabulary — Part 482: Primary and secondary cells and batteries</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>discharge</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>放電</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>排出</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「排出」（日本語）・「排放」（中国語）・「배출」（韓国語）・「Austrag」（ドイツ語）は液体・粉体などを外へ出すことで、電池から電流を取り出す放電とは別概念。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>放电</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>排放</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「排出」（日本語）・「排放」（中国語）・「배출」（韓国語）・「Austrag」（ドイツ語）は液体・粉体などを外へ出すことで、電池から電流を取り出す放電とは別概念。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>방전</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>배출</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「排出」（日本語）・「排放」（中国語）・「배출」（韓国語）・「Austrag」（ドイツ語）は液体・粉体などを外へ出すことで、電池から電流を取り出す放電とは別概念。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Entladung</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Entladen</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Austrag</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「排出」（日本語）・「排放」（中国語）・「배출」（韓国語）・「Austrag」（ドイツ語）は液体・粉体などを外へ出すことで、電池から電流を取り出す放電とは別概念。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>descarga</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-02090"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / testing-characterization</descrip><descrip type="definition">Realization of a defined quantity value with a stated measurement uncertainty, such as a standard resistor, reference voltage source or reference thermometer, used as the reference when calibrating cell test equipment.</descrip><admin type="source">JCGM 200 International vocabulary of metrology — Basic and general concepts and associated terms (VIM)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>measurement standard</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>etalon</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>測定標準</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>計量標準</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>測定規格</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「測定規格」(JA)・「norma de medición」(ES)は文書としての規格の意味になり、校正の基準器・基準値を指す本語とは別概念。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>测量标准</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>计量标准</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>측정 표준</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>측정표준</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Messnormal</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Normal</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>patrón de medida</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>patrón</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>norma de medición</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「測定規格」(JA)・「norma de medición」(ES)は文書としての規格の意味になり、校正の基準器・基準値を指す本語とは別概念。</note></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-02286"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / module-pack</descrip><descrip type="definition">Chemical hardening of an adhesive, potting compound or sealant by reaction, heat, moisture or UV until it reaches its specified strength.</descrip><admin type="source">Henkel: battery assembly adhesives, thermal interface materials and coatings (technical pages)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>curing</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>cure</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>硬化</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>固化</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>경화</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Aushärtung</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>curado</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>curación</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「curación」（ES）は傷病の治癒の意味で、接着剤・樹脂の硬化には「curado」を使う。</note></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-02289"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / module-pack</descrip><descrip type="definition">Metered application of a fluid material, such as adhesive, sealant or thermal interface material, through a nozzle in a programmed bead or dot pattern.</descrip><admin type="source">Atlas Copco: battery assembly joining, tightening and dispensing solutions (application pages)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>dispensing</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>ディスペンス</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>ディスペンサー塗布</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>調剤</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「調剤」(JA)・「配药」(ZH)は薬の調剤の意味で、接着剤・TIMの定量吐出には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>点胶</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>配药</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「調剤」(JA)・「配药」(ZH)は薬の調剤の意味で、接着剤・TIMの定量吐出には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>디스펜싱</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Dispensen</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Dosierauftrag</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>dispensado</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-02303"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / module-pack</descrip><descrip type="definition">Integral of the square of the current over the duration of a fault current, stated for a fuse as pre-arcing and operating I²t and used to coordinate battery fuses with busbars, contactors and cells.</descrip><admin type="source">IEC 60269 Low-voltage fuses (series)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>I2t value</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>I²t value</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Joule integral</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>I²t値</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>ジュール積分</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>I²t值</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>焦耳积分</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>I²t 값</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>줄 적분</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>I²t-Wert</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Joule-Integral</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>valor I²t</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>integral de Joule</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-02356"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / bms-electrical</descrip><descrip type="definition">Integrated circuit in a BMS that measures the voltages of a series string of cells, and often temperatures, with high accuracy, provides balancing switches and passes the data to the controller.</descrip><admin type="source">Texas Instruments: battery management ICs product pages and application notes</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>analog front end</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>AFE</term><termNote type="termType">abbreviation</termNote><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>battery monitoring IC</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>アナログフロントエンド</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>模拟前端</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>아날로그 프런트 엔드</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>아날로그 프론트엔드</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>analoges Frontend</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Analog-Frontend</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>front-end analógico</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-02537"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / bms-electrical</descrip><descrip type="definition">Part of a conductive EV charging coupler attached to the flexible charging cable, which mates with the vehicle inlet.</descrip><admin type="source">IEC 62196 Plugs, socket-outlets, vehicle connectors and vehicle inlets – Conductive charging of electric vehicles (series)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>vehicle connector</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>車両コネクタ</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>车辆插头</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>车辆插座</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「车辆插座」は中国語（GB/T 20234）で vehicle inlet（車両側の受け口）を指す別概念。「Fahrzeugstecker」はドイツ語（DIN EN 62196）で vehicle inlet の正式表記で、vehicle connector に使うと逆になる。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>차량 커넥터</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Fahrzeugkupplung</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Fahrzeugstecker</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「车辆插座」は中国語（GB/T 20234）で vehicle inlet（車両側の受け口）を指す別概念。「Fahrzeugstecker」はドイツ語（DIN EN 62196）で vehicle inlet の正式表記で、vehicle connector に使うと逆になる。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>conector de vehículo</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-02538"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / bms-electrical</descrip><descrip type="definition">Part of a conductive EV charging coupler built into the vehicle, into which the vehicle connector is inserted.</descrip><admin type="source">IEC 62196 Plugs, socket-outlets, vehicle connectors and vehicle inlets – Conductive charging of electric vehicles (series)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>vehicle inlet</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>車両インレット</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>车辆插座</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>车辆插头</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「车辆插头」は中国語（GB/T 20234）で vehicle connector（ケーブル側）を指す別概念。「Fahrzeugkupplung」はドイツ語（DIN EN 62196）で vehicle connector の正式表記で、vehicle inlet には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>차량 인렛</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Fahrzeugstecker</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Ladedose</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Fahrzeugkupplung</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「车辆插头」は中国語（GB/T 20234）で vehicle connector（ケーブル側）を指す別概念。「Fahrzeugkupplung」はドイツ語（DIN EN 62196）で vehicle connector の正式表記で、vehicle inlet には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>entrada de vehículo</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-02614"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / safety-abuse</descrip><descrip type="definition">Compressive load applied by the crush plate to a cell, module or pack in a crush test, used as one of the limits at which the plate is stopped.</descrip><admin type="source">GB 38031-2020 Electric vehicles traction battery safety requirements</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>crush force</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>crush load</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>圧壊荷重</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>圧壊力</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>破砕力</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「破砕力」（日本語）の破砕は電池リサイクルなどで材料を細かく砕く処理の語で、圧壊試験で押し板がセルに加える荷重には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>挤压力</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>압착력</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Quetschkraft</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>fuerza de aplastamiento</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-02641"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / safety-abuse</descrip><descrip type="definition">Cell or battery voltage above the upper limit set by the manufacturer, usually caused by overcharge or a charger fault.</descrip><admin type="source">Reddy T.B. (ed.), Linden's Handbook of Batteries, 4th ed., McGraw-Hill (2011)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>overvoltage</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>over-voltage</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>過電圧</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>过电压</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>过压</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>过电位</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>中国語の「过电位」は電極反応の過電位（overpotential）を指す電気化学の用語で、電圧が上限を超える過電圧には「过电压」を使う。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>과전압</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Überspannung</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>sobretensión</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-02674"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / safety-abuse</descrip><descrip type="definition">Gas CO2 that forms a major part of the vent gas of lithium-ion cells in thermal runaway, produced by oxidation and decomposition of carbonate electrolyte.</descrip><admin type="source">UL 9540A Test Method for Evaluating Thermal Runaway Fire Propagation in Battery Energy Storage Systems</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>carbon dioxide</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>CO2</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>二酸化炭素</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>二氧化碳</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>이산화탄소</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Kohlendioxid</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Kohlenstoffdioxid</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>dióxido de carbono</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-02824"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / quality-inspection</descrip><descrip type="definition">Feature in an X-ray or CT image that does not exist in the object, such as streaks from metal parts, beam hardening or ring artifacts, which can be mistaken for defects.</descrip><admin type="source">ISO 15708-1 Non-destructive testing - Radiation methods for computed tomography - Part 1: Terminology</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>image artifact</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>artifact</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>artefact</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>アーチファクト</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>アーティファクト</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>伪影</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>人工制品</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>中国語の「人工制品」は artifact を人工物の意味で訳した辞書訳で、X線・CT画像の偽像には「伪影」を使う。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>아티팩트</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Bildartefakt</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Artefakt</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>artefacto de imagen</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-02874"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / quality-inspection</descrip><descrip type="definition">Physical, chemical or other process that leads to a failure, such as lithium plating, SEI growth, gas generation or weld fatigue in a cell or battery.</descrip><admin type="source">IEC 60050-192:2015 International Electrotechnical Vocabulary - Part 192: Dependability</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>failure mechanism</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>故障メカニズム</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>失效机理</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>고장 메커니즘</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Ausfallmechanismus</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>mecanismo de fallo</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>mecanismo de falla</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-02940"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / dry-room-facility</descrip><descrip type="definition">Central unit housing fans, coils, filters and dampers that conditions and moves air for rooms; for dry rooms combined with a desiccant dehumidifier.</descrip><admin type="source">ASHRAE Handbook — HVAC Applications (chapter: Clean Spaces)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>air handling unit</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>AHU</term><termNote type="termType">abbreviation</termNote><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>air handler</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>エアハンドリングユニット</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>空气处理机组</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>组合式空调机组</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>공기조화기</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>공조기</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>raumlufttechnisches Gerät</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>RLT-Gerät</term><termNote type="termType">abbreviation</termNote><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>unidad de tratamiento de aire</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>UTA</term><termNote type="termType">abbreviation</termNote><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-02958"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / dry-room-facility</descrip><descrip type="definition">Central computer system that monitors and controls building services such as HVAC, dehumidifiers, lighting and alarms across a plant.</descrip><admin type="source">ASHRAE Handbook — HVAC Applications (chapter: Clean Spaces)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>building management system</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>BMS</term><termNote type="termType">abbreviation</termNote><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>building automation system</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>BAS</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>ビル管理システム</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>ビルマネジメントシステム</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>ビルディングオートメーションシステム</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>バッテリーマネジメントシステム</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>略語 BMS が電池管理システム（battery management system）と同じため、「バッテリーマネジメントシステム」「電池管理システム」（日本語）・「电池管理系统」（中国語）・「배터리 관리 시스템」（韓国語）・「Batteriemanagementsystem」（ドイツ語）・「sistema de gestión de baterías」（スペイン語）と展開すると別概念になる。建物設備の BMS は建物管理システム。</note></termSec><termSec><term>電池管理システム</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>略語 BMS が電池管理システム（battery management system）と同じため、「バッテリーマネジメントシステム」「電池管理システム」（日本語）・「电池管理系统」（中国語）・「배터리 관리 시스템」（韓国語）・「Batteriemanagementsystem」（ドイツ語）・「sistema de gestión de baterías」（スペイン語）と展開すると別概念になる。建物設備の BMS は建物管理システム。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>楼宇管理系统</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>楼宇自控系统</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>楼宇自动化系统</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>电池管理系统</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>略語 BMS が電池管理システム（battery management system）と同じため、「バッテリーマネジメントシステム」「電池管理システム」（日本語）・「电池管理系统」（中国語）・「배터리 관리 시스템」（韓国語）・「Batteriemanagementsystem」（ドイツ語）・「sistema de gestión de baterías」（スペイン語）と展開すると別概念になる。建物設備の BMS は建物管理システム。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>빌딩 관리 시스템</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>건물 관리 시스템</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>빌딩 자동화 시스템</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>배터리 관리 시스템</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>略語 BMS が電池管理システム（battery management system）と同じため、「バッテリーマネジメントシステム」「電池管理システム」（日本語）・「电池管理系统」（中国語）・「배터리 관리 시스템」（韓国語）・「Batteriemanagementsystem」（ドイツ語）・「sistema de gestión de baterías」（スペイン語）と展開すると別概念になる。建物設備の BMS は建物管理システム。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Gebäudeleittechnik</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>GLT</term><termNote type="termType">abbreviation</termNote><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Gebäudemanagementsystem</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Batteriemanagementsystem</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>略語 BMS が電池管理システム（battery management system）と同じため、「バッテリーマネジメントシステム」「電池管理システム」（日本語）・「电池管理系统」（中国語）・「배터리 관리 시스템」（韓国語）・「Batteriemanagementsystem」（ドイツ語）・「sistema de gestión de baterías」（スペイン語）と展開すると別概念になる。建物設備の BMS は建物管理システム。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>sistema de gestión de edificios</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>sistema de automatización de edificios</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>sistema de gestión de baterías</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>略語 BMS が電池管理システム（battery management system）と同じため、「バッテリーマネジメントシステム」「電池管理システム」（日本語）・「电池管理系统」（中国語）・「배터리 관리 시스템」（韓国語）・「Batteriemanagementsystem」（ドイツ語）・「sistema de gestión de baterías」（スペイン語）と展開すると別概念になる。建物設備の BMS は建物管理システム。</note></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-02991"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / dry-room-facility</descrip><descrip type="definition">All active fire protection installed in a facility, covering detection, alarm and suppression.</descrip><admin type="source">NFPA 25 (Standard for the Inspection, Testing, and Maintenance of Water-Based Fire Protection Systems)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>fire protection system</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>消防設備</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>消防用設備</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>防火設備</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「防火設備」（日本語）は建築基準法上の防火戸・防火シャッター等の語で、検知・警報・消火を含む消防設備全体には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>消防系统</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>消防设施</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>소방설비</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>Brandschutzanlage</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>sistema de protección contra incendios</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
<conceptEntry id="BAT-03174"><descrip type="subjectField">bat / recycling-regulation</descrip><descrip type="definition">Recovery of a metal such as cobalt, nickel or copper by electrolysis of a purified solution, depositing the metal on the cathode with insoluble anodes.</descrip><admin type="source">F. Habashi (ed.), Handbook of Extractive Metallurgy (Wiley-VCH, 1997)</admin><langSec xml:lang="en"><termSec><term>electrowinning</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ja"><termSec><term>電解採取</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>電解精製</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「電解精製」（日本語）・「电解精炼」（中国語）・「전해정련」（韓国語）・「Raffinationselektrolyse」（ドイツ語）・「electrorrefinación」（スペイン語）は、粗金属の陽極を溶かして純度を上げる電解精製（electrorefining）を指す別の工程で、溶液から金属を電解析出させる電解採取には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="zh"><termSec><term>电积</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>电解沉积</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>电解精炼</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「電解精製」（日本語）・「电解精炼」（中国語）・「전해정련」（韓国語）・「Raffinationselektrolyse」（ドイツ語）・「electrorrefinación」（スペイン語）は、粗金属の陽極を溶かして純度を上げる電解精製（electrorefining）を指す別の工程で、溶液から金属を電解析出させる電解採取には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="ko"><termSec><term>전해채취</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>전해정련</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「電解精製」（日本語）・「电解精炼」（中国語）・「전해정련」（韓国語）・「Raffinationselektrolyse」（ドイツ語）・「electrorrefinación」（スペイン語）は、粗金属の陽極を溶かして純度を上げる電解精製（electrorefining）を指す別の工程で、溶液から金属を電解析出させる電解採取には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="de"><termSec><term>elektrolytische Gewinnung</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Elektrogewinnung</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">admittedTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>Raffinationselektrolyse</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「電解精製」（日本語）・「电解精炼」（中国語）・「전해정련」（韓国語）・「Raffinationselektrolyse」（ドイツ語）・「electrorrefinación」（スペイン語）は、粗金属の陽極を溶かして純度を上げる電解精製（electrorefining）を指す別の工程で、溶液から金属を電解析出させる電解採取には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec><langSec xml:lang="es"><termSec><term>electroobtención</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">preferredTerm-admn-sts</termNote></termSec><termSec><term>electrorrefinación</term><termNote type="administrativeStatus">deprecatedTerm-admn-sts</termNote><note>「電解精製」（日本語）・「电解精炼」（中国語）・「전해정련」（韓国語）・「Raffinationselektrolyse」（ドイツ語）・「electrorrefinación」（スペイン語）は、粗金属の陽極を溶かして純度を上げる電解精製（electrorefining）を指す別の工程で、溶液から金属を電解析出させる電解採取には使わない。</note></termSec></langSec></conceptEntry>
</body></text>
</tbx>
